<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
	Roadmap 032, gap A's reproducer: the 20-NPC bench as generated before 032 step 6, kept
	below this comment as it was in scenarios/bench/town01_npc_20.xosc (only the FileHeader
	description and the Story name changed). Not a benchmark any more: regenerate the bench
	with scripts/gen_npc_benchmark.py instead.

	npc_05 starts on lanelet 12083 s 10, tagged `road` in the converted Town01 but, where SSv2
	puts it (y -324.33: SSv2 reads the map's lat/lon through its TransverseMercator projector,
	not the local_x/local_y tags, which would put it 2.3 m further out), CARLA's road 7 lane 2:
	a 0.3 m shoulder against the sidewalk. The Model 3 spawns with its right wheels on the
	kerb (roll 3.6 deg) and at frame 25, westbound at 8 m/s, its front meets the pole of street
	lamp CityLamp81 (x 360.94). Before 032 step 2 a snap teleported it into the pole and PhysX
	threw it 80 m up (roadmap 024 step 7, triage row 2). Since 032 the expected result is
	npc_05 blocked at frame 25, handed to kinematic at 27 and kept on the road (z within 0.5 m
	of the ground), one NPC-side contact (npc_05 / static.pole, frame 25) and a low-priority
	G2 `C2:npc_static`; no other NPC falls back. The other 19 NPCs are the old bench's.

	Original header:

	Town01, 20 puppeteered NPC vehicles and no ego: a frame-budget benchmark (roadmap 016
	step 4). Generated by scripts/gen_npc_benchmark.py; regenerate rather than edit. Each NPC
	starts on a straight lanelet and SSv2 drives it along its lane at 8.0 m/s; swb applies
	every pose with set_transform. Succeeds after 60 s of simulation time. The
	measurement is swb's "Frame budget, whole run" line, logged at the next Initialize.
-->
